  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nIssued 256 AM MDT FRI OCT 2 2026\nA weak shortwave trough will move across the area on Monday and \nweaken the ridge, cooling temperatures by a few degrees but \noverall remaining well above normal. While moisture will be \nlimited, there will be enough for a 5 to 10% chance of showers \nand thunderstorms across the higher terrain along the Nevada \nborder and central Idaho.\n\nAs the trough departs, the ridge will rebuild to our south\nTuesday through Thursday. This will keep clear, warm, and dry \nconditions in place. However, systems moving by well to our \nnorth dampen the ridge slightly with temperatures not quite as \nwarm as Sunday and Monday. On Friday, an upper level trough will\napproach the Pacific Northwest. Temperatures are expected to \nremain warm through Friday with cooler temperatures and\nprecipitation not arriving until the weekend, but confidence on \nthe timing of this system is lower. Additionally, some models\n(particularly the GFS/GEFS) indicate potential for tropical \nmoisture ahead of Hurricane Rachel (currently south of the Baja\nCalifornia peninsula) to move into the West, but confidence on \nany impacts in our area from this possible outcome is very low.",
